=== PARITY (vs web SignalCategoryTree.tsx) ===
  Logic — faithfully ported + unit-tested:
    • CATEGORY_LABELS / CATEGORY_ORDER / categoryRank / friendlyCategoryLabel — known categories rank in
      order, unknown rank last; friendly label falls back to the raw id (`?? id`).
    • groups useMemo — group by `category`, sort each group's leaves by name ascending, order groups by
      rank then friendly label.
    • TreeSelect filterGroups — a case-insensitive group-label match keeps all leaves; otherwise only
      label-matching leaves; empty groups drop; a blank/trimmed-blank needle returns the input.
    • tri-state — group + select-all checkboxes resolve none / partial / all over the VISIBLE (filtered)
      leaves; the `{groupSelectedCount}/{total}` counter and the `{n} selected[ of {total}]` summary.
    • selection transforms — toggleLeaf; toggleGroup / toggleAllVisible add-all-or-clear-all while
      preserving selections outside the visible set (web functional-setter semantics).
    • selectAllLabel — Select all / Clear all, or Select/Clear {n} visible while searching.
    • expansion — isExpanded = isSearching || expanded; toggling is a no-op while searching (everything open).
  Composition — native primitives (no Tailwind ports): a search field (web `Input` icon + clear suffix), a
    tri-state select-all header (web header Checkbox + counts + "Clear all selected"), and a scrollable
    disclosure tree (web `role="tree"`) with SF-Symbol tri-state checkboxes (checkmark/minus/empty square),
    chevron disclosure, and a value-kind chip trailing accessory (web `renderLeafRight` non-numeric fallback).
    Recharts → none (sparkline is its own surface). Leaflet → none.
  i18n — every user-facing string from the web source resolves through the P1/S10 facade with the web
    English as the fallback: "Signal catalog", "Search signals…", "No signals available for this vehicle.",
    "Failed to load catalog", and all 12 CATEGORY_LABELS (Charging / Driving / Climate / Location /
    Powertrain / Vehicle State / Safety & Security / Media / Config / Preferences / Setting Units /
    Metadata), plus the TreeSelect chrome (Select all / Clear all / Select N visible / {n} selected /
    Clear all selected / No matches / Filter tree / Clear search) — ALL present in SignalCategoryTree.strings.
    No English literals in native code.
  a11y — the picker is one contained element with a localized tree summary ("{selected} of {total} signals
    selected", or the empty message); group headers carry "{label}, {n} of {total} selected" + an
    expanded/collapsed value; the group checkbox is "Toggle {label}"; leaf rows carry "{name}, {kind} value,
    selected/not selected" and the `.isSelected` trait; the search field + clear control are labelled; the
    skeleton pulse respects Reduce Motion; Dynamic Type via the token ramp + SF Symbols. Retry button labelled.

